      "side": 1,
      "message": "### Ambiguous File I/O Error Handling (`filecontrol.cc`)\n\n**Issue:** `getBinarySize` returns `0` upon failure to open the file.\n**Impact:** The caller cannot distinguish between an empty file (which legitimately has size `0`) and an I/O error (e.g., file not found, permission denied). \n**Recommendation:** Change the return type of `getBinarySize` to `std::optional\u003csize_t\u003e` to explicitly represent failure.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 15,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "d8fed2004e8fb6edb9673b6e6e59537ac06bc029",
