      "writtenOn": "2026-04-21T18:29:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "### Unsafe Libusb Descriptor Handling (`iapcontrol.cc`)\n\n**Issue:** In `getDeviceCount`, you retrieve the configuration descriptor without checking the return value:\n\n```c\nlibusb_get_config_descriptor(found_dev, 0, \u0026config);\nfor (int i \u003d 0; i \u003c config-\u003ebNumInterfaces; i++) { ... }\n```\n\n**Impact:** If `libusb_get_config_descriptor` fails (e.g., due to permission issues or device errors), `config` will remain uninitialized or null, leading to a segmentation fault when dereferencing `config-\u003ebNumInterfaces`. **Recommendation:** Add an error check and handle the failure gracefully:\n\n```c\nif (libusb_get_config_descriptor(found_dev, 0, \u0026config) !\u003d 0) {\n    logInfo(\"[IAP] {} - get config descriptor failed\\n\", funcName);\n    return 0;\n}\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 653,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 655,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "d8fed2004e8fb6edb9673b6e6e59537ac06bc029",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
